# The ATLAS permutation carrier for Fi23

The subgroup generated by the exact `F23G1-p31671B0` permutations.
Source: R. A. Wilson et al., ATLAS of Finite Group Representations,
https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/F23G1-p31671B0 .
Original GAP files, hashes, and the reproducible transcription are in `source/`.

The source identifies this representation with Fi23 itself. In particular,
`F24G1` denotes Fi₂₄′, whereas `F24d2G1` denotes its automorphism extension.
No cover or extension is used here. Each cycle table is shifted to zero-based
letters and inverted to convert the source right action to Lean's left action.
The carrier is a subgroup of a finite symmetric group; no presentation,
order certificate, or simplicity assertion is part of its definition.

This is an alternate sourced representation to the unfinished algebra-derived
Fischer port. No comparison isomorphism with that port is asserted.
